// Title: Execute Files with Msdeploy.exe
// Sigma ID: 646bc99f-6682-4b47-a73a-17b1b64c9d34
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Beyu Denis, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-18 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects file execution using the msdeploy.exe lolbin
// False positives:
//   - System administrator Usage
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Msdeploy/
//   - https://twitter.com/pabraeken/status/995837734379032576
//   - https://twitter.com/pabraeken/status/999090532839313408
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_msdeploy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "verb:sync" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-source:RunCommand" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-dest:runCommand") and FolderPath endswith "\\msdeploy.exe"
